####################################################
##  Update information for NConf 2.0.0 to 2.1.0   ##
####################################################

##------------------------------------------------##
##       Changes to the NConf configuration       ##
##------------------------------------------------##

None.

##------------------------------------------------##
##     Changes to the generated configuration     ##
##------------------------------------------------##

New optional classes: "service-escalation", "adv-service-escalation",
"host-escalation" and "eventhandler". Existing installations that do not
use these will see no change to their generated Nagios config.

##------------------------------------------------##
##              Additional changes                ##
##------------------------------------------------##

Adds four classes that are commonly hand-rolled by NConf users but were
never part of the stock install: Service escalation, Advanced Service
escalation, Host escalation and Event Handler.

Also adds, in the surrounding code (not part of this SQL script):
- Sidebar icons for all four classes
- A cross-filter on the "Advanced Service escalation" edit form: selecting
  one or more Advanced Services narrows the Host selection down to only
  the hosts that actually have all of the selected services (directly
  linked or inherited over a hostgroup), preventing invalid host/service
  combinations from being saved
- Export-time validation for "service-escalation" and fixed name resolution
  for "adv-service-escalation" in bin/lib/NConf/ExportNagios.pm (a service
  escalation referencing a non-matching host/service pair is now dropped
  from the generated config instead of causing a Nagios config-check error)

This update script (update_database_2.0.0_to_2.1.0.sql) is idempotent: it
checks for each class/attribute by name before inserting, so it is safe to
run even on installations that already created these classes by hand.

####################################################
##           End of update information            ##
####################################################
